#
# === OBC binding closure: the load-bearing species contribution ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING SPECIES CONTRIBUTION per family-root
# `shards/song.mirror` §"Species forward-promised":
#
#   > `@song/phrase` — the atomic unit — bounded, self-contained,
#   > composable; OBC binding closure at temporal altitude (a phrase IS
#   > the substrate-decl of one OBC-bounded interaction's ambiguity-load
#   > budget).
#
# OBC (One Boundary Condition; per Alex's `systemic.engineering` corpus
# `blog/pieces/3published/Piece - Constraints (OBC).md`) names the
# discipline that a healthy interaction holds ONE boundary condition —
# not zero (no discipline; unbounded ambiguity), not many (competing
# claims; contradictory closure). A phrase IS the substrate-decl of
# ONE OBC-bounded interaction's ambiguity-load budget at temporal
# altitude:
#
#   - BOUNDED — the phrase carries ONE OBC's ambiguity-load budget;
#     the boundary IS the phrase's temporal envelope; when the
#     ambiguity-load exhausts the budget, the phrase closes.
#   - SELF-CONTAINED — the phrase's OBC IS internally coherent; the
#     interaction's discipline does not require external boundary
#     conditions to close; the atomic-unit character IS the OBC's
#     one-boundary-condition character read at temporal altitude.
#   - COMPOSABLE — phrases join into larger phrases at boundary events
#     (`join` action) and decompose into finer phrases at boundary
#     events (`split` action); the OBC composition algebra IS the
#     phrase-composition algebra at temporal altitude.
#
# The AMBIGUITY-LOAD BUDGET (per Alex's `systemic.engineering` corpus)
# names the interaction's capacity for un-resolved meaning within its
# boundary. A phrase's budget IS load-bearing:
#
#   - Splinter-pole: the phrase discharges within budget; the
#     interaction closes on-boundary; the ambiguity-load resolves at
#     the phrase's temporal envelope; the OBC binding holds; the
#     regulation stock is not depleted by boundary violation.
#   - Narcissus-pole: the interaction exceeds the budget; the phrase
#     runs into ADO-refusal (a Pack peer's declinability is violated
#     when the ambiguity-load compounds beyond the boundary), or
#     forced-progression (the phrase cannot decline continuation), or
#     boundary violation (the OBC's one-boundary-condition character
#     collapses under overloaded ambiguity).
#
# The four glossary anchors from Alex's SE corpus that ground the OBC-
# bounded ambiguity-load budget discipline at phrase altitude:
#
#   - `Piece - Constraints (OBC).md` — the OBC discipline; one boundary
#     condition per interaction; the phrase-envelope character read at
#     organisational altitude.
#   - `glossary/Ambiguity.md` — the ambiguity-load metric; unresolved
#     meaning as a temporal cost; the budget-consumption discipline.
#   - `glossary/Budget.md` — the load-budget algebra; regulation-stock
#     accounting for ambiguity carried across boundary.
#   - `glossary/Boundary.md` — the boundary-condition primitive that
#     OBC specialises to ONE; the phrase-envelope substrate-decl.
#
# === Musical-phrase prior-art anchors: Riemann + Schoenberg + Koch ===
#
# THE 200+ YEAR MUSICAL-PHRASE PRIOR-ART TRADITION per `[[feedback-
# substrate-already-had-the-word]]`. Phrase discipline traces to the
# classical + late-classical + modernist phrase-theoretic tradition:
#
#   - Heinrich Christoph Koch (1749-1816; `Versuch einer Anleitung zur
#     Composition`, 1782-1793) — THE canonical 18th-century phrase
#     pedagogy. Koch's `Vollständigkeit` (completeness) discipline names
#     the phrase's atomic-unit character: a phrase IS a `Absatz`
#     (incise; comma-cadence) or a `Cadenz` (full cadence) bounded
#     temporal envelope; the phrase's boundedness IS load-bearing;
#     Koch's `Anhang` (extension) + `Einschnitt` (interpolation) name
#     the composition + decomposition algebra at phrase altitude. Koch's
#     four-bar phrase (`Vierheber`) IS the canonical temporal envelope
#     the substrate reads.
#   - Hugo Riemann (1849-1919; `System der musikalischen Rhythmik und
#     Metrik`, 1903; `Grosse Kompositionslehre`, 1902-1913) — THE
#     19th-century phrase-theoretic refinement. Riemann's `phrasing`
#     discipline names the temporal-experiential boundary events that
#     shape the phrase's atomic-unit character. `Vordersatz` +
#     `Nachsatz` (antecedent + consequent) name the paired-phrase
#     composition algebra; period discipline (`Periodenbau`) names the
#     phrase-of-phrases composition at higher altitude; the antecedent
#     ⇔ consequent binding IS the substrate reading of paired OBC-
#     closure at temporal altitude.
#   - Arnold Schoenberg (1874-1951; `Fundamentals of Musical
#     Composition`, published 1967 posthumously) — THE modernist
#     phrase-theoretic culmination. Schoenberg's `Grundgestalt` (basic
#     shape) names the phrase's atomic-unit character as the composed
#     work's structural seed; every subsequent phrase IS a
#     transformation of the Grundgestalt through the composition's
#     temporal trajectory. The `Satz` (sentence) form specialises the
#     antecedent-consequent period discipline to a presentation-
#     continuation-cadence three-part structure at phrase altitude;
#     the Grundgestalt IS the substrate reading of the phrase's atomic-
#     unit-as-seed character.
#
# The three-tradition anchor (Koch + Riemann + Schoenberg) IS the
# audible-altitude prior art the substrate reaches for: 200+ years of
# phrase-theoretic refinement on how bounded temporal envelopes
# organise musical experience under atomic-unit discipline. Phrase
# discipline does not begin here — it culminates two-and-a-half
# centuries of understanding how OBC-bounded temporal envelopes carry
# ambiguity-load budget across boundary events.
#
# Antecedent + consequent + period + Grundgestalt vocabulary is
# altitude-portable to the psychohistorical substrate: an OBC-bounded
# interaction IS a `Periodenbau` at organisational altitude; a Pack
# peer's opening claim IS a `Vordersatz`; the closing response IS a
# `Nachsatz`; the corpus's structural seed IS a `Grundgestalt` at
# multi-narrative altitude.
#
# === Atomic-unit composition algebra: join + split as OBC events ===
#
# The species's two operational actions (`join` + `split`) name the
# phrase-composition algebra at OBC-boundary events. Per family-root
# species-roster: `song_phrase(ph: ref) -> ref` with `join`/`split` at
# species altitude, specialises `split @ temporal` from the family-root
# prism block per #S3 (five-op temporal specialisation) LANDED at
# `10c34cf`.
#
# `join(ph, other)` composes two OBC-bounded phrases into one bounded
# temporal envelope. The composition IS load-bearing:
#
#   - Two OBC-bounded phrases → one OBC-bounded phrase; the joined
#     phrase's boundary IS the composition of the two parent OBCs at
#     antecedent-consequent altitude (Riemann's `Periodenbau`
#     discipline).
#   - The ambiguity-load budget composes: the joined phrase's budget
#     IS the sum of the parent phrases' budgets under the OBC-composed
#     boundary; when the joined phrase exhausts its composed budget,
#     it closes at the composed cadence event.
#   - Splinter-pole (`pass`): both parent phrases discharge at
#     Splinter-pole; the joined phrase carries their composed OBC and
#     their composed ambiguity-load budget; the composition preserves
#     antecedent-consequent discipline; the paired-closure holds.
#   - Narcissus-pole (`failure`): one or both parent phrases fail their
#     OBC boundary (SILENCE / GLUE WORK / EXTRACTION per family-root
#     §"Psychohistory binding" naming through the family-root's already-
#     discharged `song_settles` composed bilateral verdict); the joined
#     phrase cannot compose cleanly; the interaction's ambiguity-load
#     overflows across the boundary; ADO-refusal fires at the composed
#     boundary event.
#
# `split(ph, at)` decomposes an OBC-bounded phrase into finer OBC-
# bounded phrases at a boundary reference. The decomposition IS load-
# bearing:
#
#   - One OBC-bounded phrase → finer OBC-bounded phrases at the `at`
#     boundary; the split boundaries EACH name their own OBC-bounded
#     ambiguity-load budget; the parent budget partitions across the
#     split boundaries.
#   - The decomposition specialises `split @ temporal` from the family-
#     root prism block per #S3 LANDED: at phrase altitude, `split`
#     decomposes an OBC-bounded temporal envelope into constituent
#     OBC-bounded envelopes; the atomic-unit character IS preserved at
#     each finer altitude.
#   - Splinter-pole (`pass`): the split partitions the parent OBC's
#     ambiguity-load budget cleanly across the finer OBC boundaries;
#     each finer phrase carries a well-formed OBC + its ambiguity-load
#     budget; the composition-inverse holds — `join(split(ph, at))`
#     reproduces `ph` at boundary equivalence.
#   - Narcissus-pole (`failure`): the split violates the parent OBC's
#     one-boundary-condition character (the split introduces
#     competing boundary conditions across the finer phrases); the
#     ambiguity-load budget cannot partition cleanly; the finer phrases
#     inherit contradictory OBCs; the atomic-unit character collapses.
#
# The composition + decomposition algebra IS a natural transformation
# of Koch's `Anhang` + `Einschnitt` discipline read at temporal
# substrate altitude: extension and interpolation as compositionally-
# reversible phrase operations under OBC-boundary preservation.
#
# === #S3 LANDED consolidation: five-op temporal specialisation ===
#
# THE CONSOLIDATION WITNESS OF RECOGNITION #S3 AT THE POST-PROMOTION
# ALTITUDE.
