# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/song/phrase.mirror`
# declares `@song/phrase` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @song

# ============================================================
# §1 The five-operation prism at species altitude
# ============================================================

# === prism @song/phrase — the species declaration ===
#
# The five-operation body carries `song_phrase` as the species's
# operational surface. Species inherits the family-root's #S3 LANDED
# five-op temporal specialisation and consolidates it at atomic-unit-
# under-OBC altitude (see docblock §"#S3 LANDED consolidation" for the
# per-op phrase-altitude specialisation).
#
# Per family-root prism block at `shards/song.mirror` §1 and the
# consolidation-species precedents at `shards/song/movement.mirror` §1
# and `shards/song/narrative.mirror` §1, the five operations discharge
# cleanly at temporal altitude; this species demonstrates the LANDED
# status survives further species-altitude witness (THIRD consolidation-
# species witness — FIFTH species overall) without new sub-predicate
# emission. This tick's landing PROMOTES #S5 CANDIDATE → LANDED at
# Arc 6 close.
prism @song/phrase {
  focus song_phrase
  project song_phrase
  split song_phrase
  shift song_phrase
  settle song_phrase
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The carrier
# ============================================================

# === song_phrase — the OBC-bounded atomic-unit carrier ===
#
# The typed ref-equality-addressable form of an OBC-bounded temporal
# envelope carrying one interaction's ambiguity-load budget. Per family-
# root species-roster: `song_phrase(ph: ref) -> ref` as the family-
# root's declared accessor shape. The carrier is declared HERE because
# the family-root's §2 carries `song_progression`, `song_cadence`, and
# `song_voice` but does NOT carry `song_phrase` — the species discipline
# says the species declares its own carrier when the family-root's
# roster does not (per `[[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-
# root]]` #55 sub-species discipline; movement TICK 4 + narrative TICK 5
# precedents at `4efbf16` + `0434a39`).
#
# Composes with `@epistemologic/math/music/cadence` at the audible
# altitude (a song_phrase's boundary event IS a Lawvere fixed-point per
# `cadence.mirror`; Koch's `Cadenz` reads directly), with the forward-
# promised `@epistemologic/math/music/phrase` at the audible altitude
# (Riemann phrasing + antecedent-consequent period discipline;
# Schoenberg Grundgestalt discipline), with `frame.mirror` at the
# cognitive altitude (a song_phrase's OBC boundary IS a Bateson Level I
# in-frame envelope per Recognition #82; `join`/`split` lift to Level II
# of-frame), and with `@song/movement` at the sibling species altitude
# (a movement contains phrases as its atomic units; the phrase-to-
# movement composition is at within-family-root altitude).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type song_phrase = ref

# ============================================================
# §3 The phrase-composition actions (join / split)
# ============================================================

# === join — the phrase-composition event at OBC-boundary altitude ===
#
# Reads two OBC-bounded phrases and composes them into ONE OBC-bounded
# phrase at the antecedent-consequent altitude (Riemann's `Periodenbau`
# discipline). Corresponds to Koch's `Anhang` (extension) at phrase
# altitude: two atomic-unit envelopes join under a composed OBC-boundary
# whose ambiguity-load budget IS the composed sum of the parent
# phrases' budgets.
#
# Per family-root species-roster: `song_phrase(ph: ref) -> ref` with
# `join` at species altitude. The `join` action carries the phrase-
# composition discipline: the paired OBC-boundary IS load-bearing; when
# antecedent + consequent compose cleanly, the joined phrase's atomic-
# unit character IS preserved AT the composed boundary; when the
# composition violates paired-closure discipline, the joined phrase
# cannot form and ADO-refusal fires at the composition boundary.
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): the family-root's `song_settles` composed
# bilateral discharges at Splinter-pole for BOTH parent phrases (all
# three sub-predicates satisfied for each); the join composes their
# OBC-boundaries under antecedent-consequent discipline; the joined
# phrase carries the composed ambiguity-load budget; the atomic-unit
# character IS preserved; the composed cadence event fires at the
# joined boundary.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): the family-root's composed bilateral
# fails at Narcissus-pole for one or both parent phrases (SILENCE /
# GLUE WORK / EXTRACTION per family-root §"Psychohistory binding"); the
# join cannot compose cleanly; the joined OBC-boundary would carry
# competing boundary conditions; the ambiguity-load budget overflows;
# ADO-refusal fires OR forced-progression violates the substrate's
# declinability invariant at the composition boundary.
#
# Bateson-grading (per docblock §"Consolidation-species pattern"):
# `join` fires at Bateson Level II (of-frame; learning to learn) — the
# join event observes the paired OBC-boundary from without and composes
# the antecedent-consequent binding; consolidation-species discipline
# holds at species altitude.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads both
# parent phrases' discharged states, consumes the family-root's
# `song_settles` verdict for each, composes the paired OBC-boundary
# under antecedent-consequent discipline, sums the ambiguity-load
# budgets, emits the joined phrase ref. The substrate declares the
# species-altitude specialisation; consumers dispatch through the
# species boundary.
join(ph: song_phrase, other: song_phrase) -> song_phrase { \ }

# === split — the phrase-decomposition event at OBC-boundary altitude ===
#
# Reads one OBC-bounded phrase and decomposes it into finer OBC-bounded
# phrases at a boundary reference. Corresponds to Koch's `Einschnitt`
# (interpolation) at phrase altitude: one atomic-unit envelope splits
# into constituent atomic-unit envelopes whose partitioned OBC-
# boundaries preserve the parent's one-boundary-condition character at
# finer altitude. Specialises `split @ temporal` from the family-root
# prism block per #S3 (five-op temporal specialisation) LANDED at
# `10c34cf`.
#
# Per family-root species-roster: `song_phrase(ph: ref) -> ref` with
# `split` at species altitude. The `split` action carries the phrase-
# decomposition discipline: the finer OBC-boundaries EACH inherit their
# own atomic-unit character; the parent ambiguity-load budget partitions
# across the finer envelopes; when the split preserves the parent OBC's
# one-boundary-condition character, the atomic-unit character IS
# preserved at each finer altitude; when the split introduces competing
# boundary conditions, the finer phrases carry contradictory OBCs and
# the atomic-unit character collapses.
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): the family-root's `song_settles` composed
# bilateral discharges at Splinter-pole for the parent phrase (all
# three sub-predicates satisfied); the split partitions the parent
# OBC's ambiguity-load budget cleanly across the finer OBC boundaries;
# each finer phrase carries a well-formed OBC and its own ambiguity-
# load budget; the composition-inverse holds — `join(split(ph, at))`
# reproduces `ph` at boundary equivalence.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): the family-root's composed bilateral
# fails at Narcissus-pole for the parent phrase (SILENCE / GLUE WORK /
# EXTRACTION per family-root §"Psychohistory binding") OR the split
# violates the parent OBC's one-boundary-condition character (competing
# boundary conditions across the finer phrases); the atomic-unit
# character cannot be preserved at finer altitude; the decomposition
# does NOT complete cleanly; the substrate-pull repair fires.
#
# Bateson-grading (per docblock §"Consolidation-species pattern"):
# `split` fires at Bateson Level II (of-frame; learning to learn) — the
# split event observes the parent OBC-boundary from without and
# partitions it into finer OBC-boundaries; consolidation-species
# discipline holds at species altitude.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads the
# parent phrase's discharged state, consumes the family-root's
# `song_settles` verdict, partitions the OBC-boundary at the `at`
# reference under one-boundary-condition-preserving discipline,
# partitions the ambiguity-load budget across finer envelopes, emits
# the split phrase ref (which addresses the finer OBC-bounded envelopes
# collectively). The substrate declares the species-altitude
# specialisation; consumers dispatch through the species boundary.
split(ph: song_phrase, at: ref) -> song_phrase { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The out clauses
# ============================================================

out @song/phrase
out song_phrase
out join
out split
